          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Metadata Line"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "TLS hides WHAT you said. It does not hide WHO you talked to, WHEN, HOW MUCH, or HOW OFTEN."
        },
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "q": "Can an observer tell which video I watched?",
          "a_bullets": [
            "Yes — from segment sizes and their timing",
            "Per-title bitrate patterns are near-unique",
            "TLS pads and delays nothing by default",
            "Cover traffic is the only real defence"
          ]
        },
