    {
      "page_title": "Handbook Recap: Guarantees, Trade-offs & Pre-Ship Checks",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Whole Handbook"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "TLS wraps TCP to give confidentiality, integrity and server authentication; certificates chain a hostname to a trusted root."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "One Line",
          "text": "SNI tells the server which cert to send and leaks the hostname doing it; resumption trades a little forward secrecy for a lot of latency; and the tunnel hides your content while broadcasting your metadata."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Three Guarantees"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "cards",
          "spec": {
            "cards": [
              {
                "title": "Confidentiality",
                "lines": [
                  "AES-GCM / ChaCha20",
                  "eavesdropper reads nothing"
                ]
              },
              {
                "title": "Integrity",
                "lines": [
                  "AEAD tag per record",
                  "edits are detected"
                ]
              },
              {
                "title": "Authentication",
                "lines": [
                  "cert + signature",
                  "server only, unless mTLS"
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Trade-offs Recap"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Feature",
            "Buys",
            "Costs"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "SNI",
              "many sites, one IP",
              "leaks hostname"
            ],
            [
              "Resumption",
              "fewer RTTs",
              "weaker FS"
            ],
            [
              "0-RTT",
              "zero RTT",
              "**replayable**"
            ],
            [
              "Pinning",
              "rogue-CA defence",
              "rotation risk"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. First Debug Commands"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "openssl s_client -showcerts \\",
            "  -connect host:443 \\",
            "  -servername host </dev/null",
            "openssl x509 -noout -dates \\",
            "  -ext subjectAltName -in c.pem"
          ],
          "note": "always pass -servername, or get default cert"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Never Do This"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`verify=False` or `curl -k` shipped to prod",
            "Serving the root but not the intermediate",
            "HSTS `preload` before every subdomain is HTTPS",
            "Renewing 47-day certs by hand"
          ],
          "style": "cross"
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Before You Ship",
          "items": [
            "SSL Labs grade A, full chain served",
            "Expiry alert at 14 days",
            "CT monitor on every domain you own"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
