      "page_title": "TLS 1.2 vs 1.3: Visibility",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Certificate Visibility"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Protocol",
            "Cert Status"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "TLS 1.2",
              "Plaintext"
            ],
            [
              "TLS 1.3",
              "Encrypted"
            ]
          ],
          "highlightRow": 1
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "TLS 1.2 sends cert in the clear",
            "TLS 1.3 encrypts the certificate message",
            "Observer sees only size, not content",
            "Prevents passive fingerprinting of the cert"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. ALPN Leakage"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "ALPN is sent in ClientHello",
            "Reveals HTTP/1.1, HTTP/2, or HTTP/3",
            "Visible to any network observer",
            "Indicates the client's protocol preference"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "openssl s_client -alpn h2,http/1.1 \\",
            "  -connect host:443",
            "# ALPN is visible in ClientHello"
          ],
          "note": "ALPN is not encrypted"
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Why It Matters",
          "items": [
            "ALPN helps route traffic correctly",
            "But it leaks your protocol choice",
            "TLS 1.3 hides cert, not ALPN",
            "ECH hides both, in the inner hello"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Comparison Summary"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Feature",
            "TLS 1.2",
            "TLS 1.3"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Cert",
              "Visible",
              "Hidden"
            ],
            [
              "ALPN",
              "Visible",
              "Visible"
            ],
            [
              "SNI",
              "Visible",
              "Visible"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Key Takeaway",
          "text": "TLS 1.3 encrypts the certificate, but SNI and ALPN stay visible in both versions — only ECH moves them into an encrypted inner ClientHello."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. What ECH Changes"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Encrypts the ==inner ClientHello==: real SNI and ALPN",
            "Key comes from the domain's HTTPS DNS record",
            "Outer hello carries a **decoy** shared SNI",
            "Needs DoH/DoT too, or DNS leaks the name first"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Still Leaked With ECH"
