  "caption": {
    "text": "Part 2 of HTTPS & TLS: THE HANDSHAKE HANDBOOK. The padlock does not mean the site is safe — it means the bytes are encrypted to whoever answered the phone. This handbook walks the TLS 1.2 and 1.3 handshakes packet by packet, decodes certificate chains and SAN matching, explains why SNI still leaks every hostname you visit, and ends with the config checklist and error-triage table you actually reach for at 2am. 10 pages, no fluff: internals, trade-offs, and the misconfigurations that bite in production.",
